From 21d8de77688a72d3a23fa39acb3ab67af6a70c2c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeff Wallace <jwallace115@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 20:10:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] nfl_sim Phase 5A-6: goal-line censoring (Kaplan-Meier) in
 yardage tables, end-of-half FG decision, Q2<2 clock bucket

Cowork-executed phase (no Claude Code relay). Root cause of the K1 scoring
deficit found and fixed at the table level:

1. Yardage tables were built from RECORDED gains, which are right-censored at
   the goal line (a scoring play from the 8 records 8 yards). Pooling those
   plays into 5 field zones biased the drawn gain downward for the deeper end
   of every zone: TD rate per completion from the 5-10 was 26% in the sim vs
   53% real; 40+ completions 0.73/game vs 0.97. tables.py now estimates each
   cell's UNCONSTRAINED gain distribution with Kaplan-Meier (scoring plays =
   censored at yardline_100), borrowing the unobservable tail from the next
   zone out (open field for midfield/own zones). No constants; every quantile
   is an observed gain or the sentinel the engine caps at the goal line.
   Per-play TD rates by yardline now match reality within a few points at
   every bin; offensive TDs 3.94 -> 4.82/game (actual 4.73).

2. End-of-half FG on downs 1-3 (new empirical table J, eoh_fg_decision):
   real teams kick before the half expires on any down (0.33 att/game, ~90%
   of them with <=10s left). Engine only considered FGs on 4th down.

3. Q2<2 clock bucket in the play-call and 4th-down tables: last 2:00 of Q2
   is a two-minute drill (pass rate 0.80 vs 0.58 pooled Q1-3; FG rate in
   range ~10pp higher). Was pooled into Q1-3.

Diagnostic counters added (ev_fg_non4th, ev_eoh_snaps, ev_late_snaps_q2/q4,
ev_pass_40, ev_rush_20, ev_td_long, ev_td_short) and a module-level
_DEBUG_YDS collector for per-play yardage audits.

Tests: nfl/sim/tests/test_engine_5a6.py (8 tests at spec tolerance, all
passing). K1 before/after and report in the follow-up docs commit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QMk9gfHmH2aTN5pwMcY52R
